== 3. Drift rule, Delta_0 and the label ==
  J5 drift rule on the J5 stand-in against 61c's constants: tmin108 45.960 (|d| 0.000 <= 0.3), u108 0.948 (|d| 0.001 <= 0.02) -> DRIFT-OK (it must read DRIFT-OK on its own reference rows)
  J0 stand-in: need_0 7.232 [6.829, 7.925], need_5 (law's pair, J5 cell) 3.481, Delta_0 0.972, D0 7.072 -> LABEL62 NEED0 UNSCOREABLE (floor count drop D0 >= 0.5 ms)
  the same with the gate forced open (exercise only; not a reading): LABEL62 NEED0 UNRESOLVED
  (with the gate failing, need_0 carries the floor's count drop: here need_0 - need_law(J0 stand-in) = 3.462 ms, which is why the gate exists)
  band check: 2 Delta_0 = 1.94 < need_5 = 3.48: disjoint

== 4. The label function on every branch (SYNTHETIC inputs; need_5 4.0, Delta_0 1.05) ==
  spread       CI (-0.3, 0.4) D0 0.1 n 6 -> SPREAD-CARRIED
  constant     CI (3.6, 4.3) D0 0.1 n 6 -> CONSTANT
  intermediate CI (1.4, 2.0) D0 0.1 n 6 -> INTERMEDIATE
  straddle     CI (0.8, 1.6) D0 0.1 n 6 -> UNRESOLVED
  gate         CI (3.6, 4.3) D0 0.7 n 6 -> UNSCOREABLE (floor count drop D0 >= 0.5 ms)
  replicates   CI (3.6, 4.3) D0 0.1 n 4 -> UNSCOREABLE (fewer than 5 replicates with W95 in [K1, K3])

